# Ulo public app URLs — one builder

Every feature that needs a **website** link (SMS, email, Connect return, deep link) must use the shared helpers — do not concatenate `APP_URL` / `window.location.origin` + path in feature code.

## APIs

| Runtime | Module |
|---|---|
| Edge | `supabase/functions/_shared/uloAppUrl.ts` → `uloAppOrigin`, `uloAppUrl.*` |
| Client | `src/lib/uloAppUrl.ts` → `uloAppOrigin`, `uloAppUrl.*` |

Named routes:

| Helper | Path |
|---|---|
| `uloAppUrl.vendorVerification(token)` | `/v/:token` |
| `uloAppUrl.rentPayment({ runId, residentId, billingPeriod, amountDue })` | `/pay/rent?...` |
| `uloAppUrl.workOrder(token)` | `/w/:token` |
| `uloAppUrl.estimate(token)` | `/estimate/:token` |
| `uloAppUrl.invoice(token)` | `/invoice/:token` |
| `uloAppUrl.upload(token)` | `/upload/:token` |
| `uloAppUrl.admin(path?)` | `/admin` or `/admin/...` |
| `uloAppUrl.absolute(path)` | any other app path |

Connect return/refresh base: `resolveConnectAppBaseUrl` (delegates to `uloAppOrigin`) or `uloAppOrigin({ returnOrigin, requestOrigin, fallback: "" })`.

## Do not

- Rebuild `APP_URL + "/v/" + token` (or estimate/invoice/upload/work-order) in new feature code
- Put **Stripe Checkout session URLs** or **`…/functions/v1/…` invoke URLs** into this helper — those are not public app pages
- URL-encode Stripe’s `{CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}` placeholder (keep it literal in success_url)

## When adding a new public page

1. Add a named helper on `uloAppUrl` (edge + client)
2. Call it from SMS/email/Connect/deep-link builders
3. Keep path shapes identical across runtimes
